  "implementation_notes": [
    "Intervals are half-open abstract coordinates and must be order-preservingly mapped to serialized SNI-relative byte endpoints.",
    "In the default TTL family forwarded means delivered internally to the DPI analyzer, not to Linux. Linux has no data ACK frontier advance.",
    "The paper's normalization algorithm deliberately removes uncommon geometries. Do not apply it as the unknown DPI oracle.",
    "At most two geometric holes means maximal missing components before the largest received endpoint; do not count the future suffix.",
    "A fixed prefix that was analyzed can be represented separately from buffered bytes; do not let a later conflicting byte undo a latched censor bit.",
    "Bare interval overlap does not imply conflicting bytes. Payload synthesis must create equal-length hostname disagreements within overlapping SNI positions.",
    "A letter label indicates geometric coverage only, never a measured behavioral fingerprint."
  ],
